 istorical acceptance covers main full papers only\, not Blue Sky Ideas or
  the newly introduced 2027 Findings track.\nScope: Autonomous agents and 
 multi-agent systems: learning and adaptation\, coordination\, game theory
 \, planning\, reasoning\, agent engineering\, and agent-based simulation.
  Also covers human-agent interaction\, robot teams\, norms and governance
 \, and generative agents. The contribution should concern agents or their
  interaction\; generic language-model or learning results are not automat
 ically in scope.\nAdditional topics: Deep Representation Learning\, Proba
 bilistic\, Causal & Uncertainty ML\, Control & Robotics\, Complex Systems
  & Network Science\, Ethics & Governance\, Explainability & Interpretabil
 ity\nScope sources (2027): https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas2027/ca
 lls/call-for-main-track/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/dcs/aamas2027/calls/call-for-blue-sky-ide
 as/
